KG42.register("clusters-2d2627bb1e2568fcd645a5a3",{"id":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v142-d-CL001","paper":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading","label":"Power purchase declaration and supplier selection under price conditions","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Power purchase declaration and supplier selection under price conditions","market_meaning":"When the current price is fixed, the microgrid determines its power purchase request and supplier set based on local load, marginal cost, and applicable cases, and discloses the request to the corresponding sellers. The positive-load and zero-load branches are retained separately; existing mathematical issues mean that this candidate cannot yet serve as a complete local closed-form decision rule.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","matching"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The two chains describe the quantity and supplier selection of the same local subproblem. Case 2 and Case 3 are limited to positive load; zero load is handled according to the existing extension. The same-form set expression does not remove the complete premises of the different cases, nor does it prove that the branches are mutually exclusive and exhaustive.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The supplier set directly defines the nonzero coordinates of the power purchase quantity, so together they constitute the power purchase decision; no separate matching procedure is set up on that basis. Generation, electricity sales, and global price adjustment are still handled through other clusters.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the power purchase quantity under a fixed price, branch conditions, non-negativity, and request disclosure."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplements the supplier grouping and directed-connection restrictions of the same power purchase decision."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g32-e032","v141-b-g34-e034","v141-b-g35-e035","v141-b-g37-e037"],"rationale":"Each supplier set corresponds respectively to the power purchase quantity coordinates of the same case; assembly is performed only according to the corresponding branch, retaining all conditions and the zero-load exception."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x_E_ji"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-X001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g06-e006","v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g34-e034"],"rationale":"Under the same buyer i, seller j, and price snapshot, the declared quantity is also a power purchase coordinate restricted by supplier selection; this correspondence does not interpret the iterative request as delivered energy."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.inter_area","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.inter_area"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::pricing.inter_area","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g38-e038"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the inter-microgrid price function of the same mechanism; the representative selection is used only for display."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x_E_ji","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g06-e006","v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g34-e034"],"rationale":"In the same local case, they refer to the power purchase quantity in the same direction, retaining the declaration and supplier screening roles respectively."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_i","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g38-e038"],"rationale":"Both are the local microgrid selling price fixed in the same local solution, retaining their respective parameter bindings."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_j","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-T002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g26-e026","v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g38-e038"],"rationale":"Only under the same buyer, supplier, and local snapshot do they correspond to the neighboring party's purchase price; the infinite-price convention when there is no incoming connection continues to be retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The η definition formula in Case 3 and the power purchase quantity expression use different symbols for the neighboring party's price, and the supplier grouping chain cannot eliminate this inconsistency.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g32-e032"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original formula and have the upstream clarify the symbols and applicable conditions; this round retains the frozen expression and does not claim on that basis that the mathematics of Case 3 is closed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The consistency between the last-term load comparison in Case 2 and the conclusion of no generation, and whether the premises of Case 5 are sufficient to guarantee nonnegative electricity sales, still need to be checked. The current two chains do not carry the corresponding complete generation and electricity sales branches, and these conclusions cannot be confirmed solely from the power purchase and grouping expressions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g16-e016","v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g34-e034"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the inequality direction and branch boundaries against the local feasible region, complete branch results, and KKT conditions; if supplementation is needed, leave it to C and do not add new conditions in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The existing general cost assumptions provide only properties such as convexity and are not sufficient by themselves to guarantee that marginal cost is globally invertible and that η is unique; the properties claimed in these sources still lack an explicit applicable domain and sufficient conditions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_Gamma","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_eta","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g11-e011","v141-b-g27-e027","v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g32-e032"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the domain of the inverse function, the strength of monotonicity required, and the conditions for existence and uniqueness of the auxiliary solution, and then check branch coverage; do not strengthen the cost assumptions on your own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"This cluster is assembled based on unaudited citations permitted by the experiment; B's source_status remains unverified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g31-e031","v141-b-g32-e032","v141-b-g34-e034","v141-b-g35-e035","v141-b-g37-e037","v141-b-g38-e038"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original text, branch conditions, and mathematical transcription item by item; the current assembly does not indicate that the source or scientific conclusions have been independently reviewed."}]},"rule_refs":["27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R001","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-29a9bef8bb03bc72","KG40-4b961454dc326f08","KG40-7b5176e5e40aa7c7"]});
